{"name":"Shiny Kettle","hex":"#cea190","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shiny","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Reflecting light.","Emitting light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Anything that glitters; a trinket.","A desirable collectible."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shiny"},{"term":"kettle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vessel for boiling a liquid or cooking food, usually metal and equipped with a lid.","The quantity held by a kettle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To contain demonstrators in a confined area.","Of a boiler: to make a whistling sound like the boiling of a kettle, indicative of various types of fault."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kettle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kettle","blocks":[{"text":"A kettle, sometimes called a tea kettle or teakettle, is a device specialized for boiling water, commonly with a lid, spout, and handle. There are two main types: the stovetop kettle, which uses heat from a hob, and the electric kettle, which is a small kitchen appliance with an internal heating element. Kettles are used mainly in the preparation of hot beverages, but also in food preparation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Bernadotte_Wasserkessel.jpg/330px-Bernadotte_Wasserkessel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettle","wikidata":"Q107444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG/500px-Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Electric_kettle_-_%D